## Directory Structure

- `cypress/e2e`: specifications organized by module. The `specPattern` in `cypress.config.js` ensures execution order. **See [ADR-0007](../docs/adr/0007-separate-specs-by-functionality-and-type.md)**
- `cypress/support/pages`: Page Object classes with interaction logic. **See [ADR-0002](../docs/adr/0002-use-page-object-pattern.md)** and [ADR-0008](../docs/adr/0008-use-page-object-hierarchy.md)
- `cypress/support/locators`: files that centralize selectors. **See [ADR-0003](../docs/adr/0003-separate-locators-from-page-objects.md)**
- `cypress/support/factory`: data factories built with Faker. **See [ADR-0009](../docs/adr/0009-use-faker-for-dynamic-test-data.md)**
- `cypress/support/commands.js`: utility commands (login, menu navigation, validations).
- `cypress/support/e2e.js`: loads plugins (Allure, cypress-xpath, Percy, cypress-grep) and global hooks.
- `cypress/fixtures`: static test data.
- `docs/cases/`: architecture documentation for each spec. **See [ADR-0006](../docs/adr/0006-mandatory-documentation-for-new-tests.md)**
- `allure-results` and `allure-report`: test reports. **See [ADR-0005](../docs/adr/0005-use-allure-for-test-reporting.md)**

---

## Main Configuration

- `cypress.config.js`: `baseUrl`, `viewport` 1366x768, `defaultCommandTimeout` 50s.
- `setupNodeEvents`: registers `allure-cypress` and `@cypress/grep`.
- `testIsolation: false` preserves states between tests.

---

## Execution Flows

**npm scripts:**
- `npm run e2e`: runs Cypress with Allure enabled
- `npm run test:chrome|test:firefox`: specific browser
- `npm run test:allure`: generates and opens Allure report
- `npm run lint`: validates ESLint standards

