## Validation and Quality

### Continuous Validation Checklist

> **Context**: See [ADR-0013](../docs/adr/0013-continuous-validation-checklist.md)

**Use this checklist during code review to ensure continuous ADR compliance:**

#### Quick Validation Checklist

1. **ADR-0002 (Page Objects):**
   - [ ] No CSS/XPath selectors directly in spec
   - [ ] UI interactions encapsulated in Page Objects

2. **ADR-0003 (Locators):**
   - [ ] Locators in separate files
   - [ ] File name in PascalCase
   - [ ] Locators use IDs when available
   - [ ] Locators have appropriate context (modal, panel)
   - [ ] Locators were validated in browser
   - [ ] Locators are not too generic
   - See [Locators Best Practices](#35-locators-best-practices) for details

3. **ADR-0004 (Login):**
   - [ ] Correct login command (fiscal vs non-fiscal)
   - [ ] Uses `cy.session()` for caching

4. **ADR-0010 (Tags):**
   - [ ] Tags applied in `describe`
   - [ ] Tags follow pattern: `['@modulo', '@tipo', '@regressivo']`

5. **ADR-0006 (Documentation):**
   - [ ] Architecture documentation created
   - [ ] `docs/testes.md` updated
   - [ ] `docs/cases/README.md` updated

6. **Code Simplification:**
   - [ ] No code duplication
   - [ ] Unused code removed
   - [ ] Selectors centralized (no hardcoded selectors)
   - [ ] No fixed waits (use conditional validations)
   - [ ] Complexity managed (constants for magic numbers)
   - See [Code Simplification Best Practices](#36-code-simplification-best-practices) for details

**Complete Checklist:** `docs/referencias/checklist-validacao-continua.md`

### Page Object Hierarchy Guidelines

> **Context**: See [ADR-0008](../docs/adr/0008-use-page-object-hierarchy.md)

### When to Use Hierarchy

✅ **Use hierarchy when:**
- Module has 3+ variants with significant common functionality
- Common methods represent >30% of total methods
- Variants share complex workflows (e.g., items, payments, emission)
- Maintenance of common code is difficult without hierarchy

❌ **Do NOT use hierarchy when:**
- Only 1-2 variants exist
- Variants are very different
- Common methods are minimal (<30% of total methods)
- Hierarchy adds more complexity than value

### Recommended Structure

```
Module/
├── ModuleBasePage.js           # Base class (common methods)
├── ModuleVariant1Page.js      # Inherits from Base
└── ModuleVariant2Page.js      # Inherits from Base
```

**Maximum:** 2 levels of inheritance (Base → Specific)

### Current Implementation Status

- ✅ **NFe module** - Fully implemented and compliant
  - Structure: `CadastroNfeBasePage` → `CadastroNfeNormalBasePage` → Specific classes
  - Maximum 2 levels of inheritance
  - Facade pattern used for backward compatibility

**Reference:** `docs/referencias/analise-page-objects-hierarquicos.md` for complete analysis

